"id":2765837432,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6k21R4","user":{"login":"mrimvo","id":6030346,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMzAzNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6030346?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrimvo","html_url":"https://github.com/mrimvo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrimvo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrimvo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrimvo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrimvo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrimvo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrimvo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrimvo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrimvo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrimvo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-31T10:38:30Z","updated_at":"2025-03-31T10:39:12Z","body":"> Sounds like a duplicate\n\nno, not a duplicate. the other ticket discusses `@export` Resources, this ticket is about `@export` Dictionary.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2765837432/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2765880979","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103314#issuecomment-2765880979","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103314","id":2765880979,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6k2_6T","user":{"login":"monitz87","id":7144213,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDQyMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7144213?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87","html_url":"https://github.com/monitz87","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-31T11:00:01Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T09:58:02Z","body":"This behavior is highly unintuitive and can lead to unexpected and almost impossible to debug scenarios in more complex systems","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2765880979/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2767884210","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103314#issuecomment-2767884210","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103314","id":2767884210,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6k-o-y","user":{"login":"drearyweary","id":87843427,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODQzNDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87843427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary","html_url":"https://github.com/drearyweary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T02:21:39Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T02:21:39Z","body":"> Minimal code snipped to reproduce this:\n> \n> your_scene.tscn: `@export var dict := {}`\n> \n> Then set a value using the Inspector.\n> \n> Somewhere else:\n> \n> ```\n> \tvar Scene: PackedScene = load(\"your_scene.tscn\")\n> \tvar scene1 = Scene.instantiate()\n> \tvar scene2 = Scene.instantiate()\n> \n> \tscene1.dict[\"my_test\"] = 12\n> \n> \t# BUG: changing dict in scene1 changes dict in scene 2!\n> \tvar bug = \"my_test\" in scene2.dict\n> ```\n\nActually, I believe this snippet is exhibiting correct behavior because of reference counting on the dictionary from Scene. So the dictionary in scene1 and scene2 being in the same script here will reference count the dictionary from Scene currently loaded in memory and reflect any similar changes across any of them.\n\nMy MRP issue occurs when I change an exported dictionary in a preload in one scene, change to another scene with a different script and load that previously preloaded tscn. When in another scene altogether, I didn't expect the changed exported dictionary and array to still persist. I was under the impression that once a previous scene has freed with any preloaded resources, the reference counting ends and starts anew if loaded again.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2767884210/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768924172","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103314#issuecomment-2768924172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103314","id":2768924172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lCm4M","user":{"login":"monitz87","id":7144213,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDQyMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7144213?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87","html_url":"https://github.com/monitz87","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T10:34:26Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T10:43:52Z","body":"> Actually, I believe this snippet is exhibiting correct behavior\n\nWhile the behavior might make \"sense\" given how packed scenes are loaded, it is highly unintuitive and breaks the principle of least astonishment IMO. Developers that come from any other language will expect that independent instances of the same scene would not share data containers unless said containers are static or explicitly assigned to a common value.\n\nAt least for resources we have `local_to_scene` to control this behavior. There's no such thing for dictionaries or arrays\n\n> My MRP issue occurs when I change an exported dictionary in a preload in one scene, change to another scene with a different script and load that previously preloaded tscn. When in another scene altogether, I didn't expect the changed exported dictionary and array to still persist. I was under the impression that once a previous scene has freed with any preloaded resources, the reference counting ends and starts anew if loaded again.\n\nBtw, this might be related to the resource cache. As long as there is an existing reference to a given loaded resource, calling `load` and `preload` will just return said instance*. If something in your code is keeping the PackedScene reference alive while you're switching scenes, then the behavior you're seeing makes sense (in the same between air quotes connotation of sense I'm using in my previous paragraph). I imagine you can see how ugly it is to have (potentially) wildly different behavior depending on whether a cache entry for a resource exists or not. Developers shouldn't have to worry about the cache affecting actual game logic.\n\n*: you could verify that this is what is going on by replacing your `preload` and `load` with `ResourceLoader.load(resource_path, \"\", CACHE_MODE_IGNORE_DEEP)`. If that change makes the issue go away, then it is very likely that I'm right\n\nP.S.: if the issue *is* the cache, but you're quite sure that you're not keeping any references after switching scenes, then you probably found another bug","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768924172/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2780549424","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103314#issuecomment-2780549424","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103314","id":2780549424,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lu9Ew","user":{"login":"drearyweary","id":87843427,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODQzNDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87843427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary","html_url":"https://github.com/drearyweary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-05T08:08:34Z","updated_at":"2025-04-05T08:08:34Z","body":"> *: you could verify that this is what is going on by replacing your `preload` and `load` with `ResourceLoader.load(resource_path, \"\", CACHE_MODE_IGNORE_DEEP)`. If that change makes the issue go away, then it is very likely that I'm right\n\nBy replacing the 'preload' with the 'ResourceLoader.load' method (have to change it from a constant to a variable for load to not throw an error), the issue goes away. Similarly, as stated in my original post, replacing 'preload' with the normal 'load', solves the issue. So something is happening with preloads that keeps it in some cache that I am not familiar with.\n\nMy script is very simple and self contained with no global links or external dependencies, except for that preloaded packed scene. Thus, I assumed that once switched to another scene, any references would be freed. But that preload with an editor altered exported array and dictionary somehow persists between scenes. I even tried to add more scene changes in between to no avail.\n\nInterestingly, I thought the preload being a constant (thus having an unchanging Object ID) was what kept it in memory. But when I changed it to a 'var' with a preload, the issue still persists.\n\nI've narrowed the steps to reproduce the issue down to:\n\n- a preloaded packed scene (can be a var or const)\n- this packed scene must contain an exported array or dictionary whose values have been modified in editor (default values do not create this issue)\n- these values are passed by reference to another array or dictionary in a running game\n- the passed values are then changed in the same running game, causing exported values in packed scene to change by reference and persist in memory regardless of how many scene changes\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2780549424/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807043836","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103314#issuecomment-2807043836","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103314","id":2807043836,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nUBb8","user":{"login":"monitz87","id":7144213,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDQyMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7144213?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87","html_url":"https://github.com/monitz87","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monitz87/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T17:59:42Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T18:00:53Z","body":"I think preloads are done on project startup, so it might make sense that they're cached at a global level (since the engine can't possibly know when an object with the script that contains the preload will be instantiated, how many times, and when it will cease to be instantiated)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2807043836/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2808461053","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103314#issuecomment-2808461053","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103314","id":2808461053,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nZbb9","user":{"login":"drearyweary","id":87843427,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODQzNDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87843427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary","html_url":"https://github.com/drearyweary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drearyweary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T06:00:15Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T06:00:15Z","body":"> I think preloads are done on project startup, so it might make sense that they're cached at a global level (since the engine can't possibly know when an object with the script that contains the preload will be instantiated, how many times, and when it will cease to be instantiated)\n\nThat's what I've suspected as well, which would logically allow the behavior I'm seeing to happen. Although, I have also seen people say otherwise, but I'm not proficient in C++ enough to look at the source code to verify any of this.\n\nMy current solution is to never modify reference counted resources or items in preloaded scenes.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2808461053/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2838642150","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103314#issuecomment-2838642150","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103314","id":2838642150,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pMj3m","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-29T12:31:30Z","updated_at":"2025-04-29T12:31:30Z","body":"Linking in #87351 since I suspect a similar root cause.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2838642150/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]